<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.27 bln on Oct 18.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.27 bln on Oct 18.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.27 billion on October 18, 1996, from $23.19 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Oct 18	Oct 11	 Oct 20</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     18,839	18,764	 18,526</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,410	 4,410	  4,405</p>
<p>    SDRs				    18	    18	    308</p>
<p>    Total			     23,267	23,192	 23,239</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
